WEBVTT

00:59.210 --> 01:03.010
Chris, what is it?

01:04.410 --> 01:08.210
I love you so much.

01:09.710 --> 01:12.810
Don't you love me any more?

01:25.210 --> 01:29.110
I've made progress,
and I recognize that.

01:29.610 --> 01:35.210
But my wife, who I can't
even convince to come here...

01:35.610 --> 01:39.210
Anything can set her off.
It could be the phone ringing,

01:39.610 --> 01:43.610
something on the news,
something online, going shopping maybe.

01:44.010 --> 01:48.510
A commemorative T-shirt in the window.
It just puts her right back in that place,

01:48.910 --> 01:53.810
and it's like all my progress - ripped away.
And I'm right back there with her.

01:54.310 --> 01:59.410
I feel totally the opposite. I see the TV
and I see the Internet and I see those T-shirts

01:59.810 --> 02:05.810
and I feel nothing. The more I see the images,
the less I feel, the less I believe that it's real.

02:06.310 --> 02:12.310
I mean, I think I'm supposed to feel
something by now. Don't you think so?

02:14.510 --> 02:18.010
Linda, this is Chris Kelvin.
I'm returning your call.

02:18.510 --> 02:21.410
I have two times available this week;

02:21.710 --> 02:26.510
7am on Tuesday
or 6.15pm on Thursday.

02:27.010 --> 02:33.510
You can leave a message if either
of those times are good for you. Thank you.

02:34.010 --> 02:36.610
Well, I know that's not true.

02:37.010 --> 02:41.710
Because I know you, and I know it's not true.

02:46.410 --> 02:48.910
Good. I'm glad.

02:49.310 --> 02:50.910
All right.

02:51.210 --> 02:55.110
Let's pick this up on Wednesday.

03:59.210 --> 04:01.610
Can I help you?

04:02.010 --> 04:06.210
We're looking for Dr Chris Kelvin.

04:10.610 --> 04:13.710
Chris...

04:15.110 --> 04:19.910
I can't imagine what you must be
thinking, getting a message like this.

04:20.310 --> 04:27.010
I apologise if it seems melodramatic, but
you are the only person I can... I can trust...

04:27.610 --> 04:30.810
in the situation.

04:31.210 --> 04:33.610
I need your help.

04:33.910 --> 04:36.410
I need you to come to Solaris, Chris.

04:36.910 --> 04:40.710
I don't know how to describe
what we are experiencing up here.

04:41.010 --> 04:46.210
We can't even agree amongst ourselves
what is... what is happening, or...

04:46.810 --> 04:50.510
what to do about it.

04:51.210 --> 04:57.210
I suppose the... the most obvious
solution would be to leave.

04:57.710 --> 05:04.410
But none of us want to. That's why
you're getting this... this bizarre request.

05:04.910 --> 05:07.710
I...

05:08.110 --> 05:11.910
I told the crew that your
background and experiences

05:12.310 --> 05:17.310
made you the...
the ideal candidate for this job.

05:17.810 --> 05:20.010
Don't worry. I didn't elaborate.

05:21.910 --> 05:24.610
But it's true.

05:25.010 --> 05:28.410
So, anyway...

05:30.010 --> 05:33.410
I, uh... I hope you will come to Solaris, Chris.

05:33.810 --> 05:36.410
L- I think you need to.

05:36.810 --> 05:39.910
You will see what I mean.

05:40.410 --> 05:46.510
I wish I could be more specific
about all of this, but... you know.

05:47.110 --> 05:50.910
People are listening.

05:54.610 --> 06:00.810
You can imagine the distress
Dr Gibarian's message caused at DBA.

06:03.210 --> 06:05.610
Why not send in the security force?

06:05.910 --> 06:10.310
We did. We lost contact
as they were approaching Solaris.

06:10.810 --> 06:14.310
They haven't returned.

06:14.710 --> 06:17.510
There must be some
sort of on-board Al system.

06:17.810 --> 06:19.610
They shut it down.

06:19.910 --> 06:24.110
The company was hoping to solve
this problem without involving a civilian.

06:24.510 --> 06:28.810
Obviously these are extreme circumstances.

06:29.310 --> 06:32.910
Some preparation is involved
but you shouldn't have any trouble.

06:33.210 --> 06:39.510
The flight itself is fully automated.
You'll be asleep most of the trip.

06:40.710 --> 06:47.710
We feel confident that if you board
the ship, you can negotiate their safe return.

06:48.210 --> 06:51.610
Is that what everybody wants?

06:52.010 --> 06:55.510
Of course.

12:21.510 --> 12:25.410
Find the probability of F.

12:28.010 --> 12:31.910
OK, stop. Go back.

12:33.810 --> 12:37.310
Snow.

12:56.010 --> 12:59.210
Kelvin, is it?

12:59.610 --> 13:01.210
Yeah.

13:01.610 --> 13:05.310
Kelvin. Right. Oh, man.

13:05.710 --> 13:08.010
Sorry about that, Kelvin.

13:08.410 --> 13:10.410
Names, you know, just...

13:10.710 --> 13:12.810
For some reason. It, uh...

13:13.210 --> 13:15.610
Yeah. Uh...

13:15.910 --> 13:18.910
Well, uh, you wanna come in?

13:19.310 --> 13:21.410
I'm fine.

13:21.710 --> 13:26.610
Whose blood is that, leading to the lab?

13:27.110 --> 13:30.610
Yeah. Blood.

13:30.710 --> 13:34.110
How 'bout that?

13:37.410 --> 13:39.410
Katarn.

13:39.710 --> 13:41.610
He, um... Yeah.

13:41.910 --> 13:46.810
Security forces showed up
and he just took off, and they...

13:47.310 --> 13:50.510
Yeah. Put a hole in his pot.

13:50.910 --> 13:54.610
What happened to Gibarian?

13:55.910 --> 13:57.810
Yeah.

13:58.110 --> 14:01.910
It was a suicide.

14:03.110 --> 14:04.810
Who found him?

14:05.210 --> 14:08.110
I found him.

14:08.510 --> 14:11.710
What happened to Rhys?

14:12.010 --> 14:14.510
Yeah, now, Rhys w... Huh.

14:14.810 --> 14:18.910
We don't know, because the thing is,
he kind of... disappeared.

14:19.310 --> 14:21.110
- Disappeared?
- Disappeared.

14:21.410 --> 14:25.910
- How did he disappear?
- Exactly.

14:26.610 --> 14:29.710
Don't know. We do know
that he's not on the ship, uh,

14:30.010 --> 14:34.210
and that's... that's all we know.

14:34.610 --> 14:37.010
Where's Dr Gordon?

14:37.310 --> 14:40.810
Dr Gordon. She is in her room,

14:41.210 --> 14:42.910
and, um...

14:43.310 --> 14:47.510
Dr Gordon won't let you in her room.

14:51.910 --> 14:56.410
Can you tell me what's happening here?

14:57.110 --> 14:59.410
I could tell you what's happening,

14:59.810 --> 15:02.510
but, uh...

15:02.810 --> 15:08.310
I don't know if that'd
really tell you what's happening.

15:14.510 --> 15:17.510
I just wanna talk to you.

15:17.910 --> 15:23.310
You have to give me your word
you won't try to come in.

15:26.510 --> 15:30.010
All right.

15:44.610 --> 15:46.310
Well?

15:46.710 --> 15:50.410
- What happened to Gibarian?
- Didn't you talk to Snow?

15:50.710 --> 15:54.010
- I wanted to hear your version.
- There isn't any version.

15:54.410 --> 15:58.210
He killed himself.

15:59.110 --> 16:04.210
Why haven't you come home?
What happened here?

16:04.610 --> 16:08.610
What did you find?

16:08.910 --> 16:12.810
- Who are you representing?
- I'm the last effort to recover this mission,

16:13.210 --> 16:17.910
before they abandon this ship
and everyone on board.

16:26.710 --> 16:31.010
Until it starts happening to you,
there's really no point in discussing it.

16:54.910 --> 16:58.210
Hey.

17:04.510 --> 17:07.810
Hey!

17:22.710 --> 17:26.210
- Who else is here?
- Who else is here?

17:26.710 --> 17:30.210
I saw a boy.

17:33.210 --> 17:37.110
Gibarian's son.

17:37.710 --> 17:42.010
- Michael.
- How is that possible?

17:42.510 --> 17:45.410
I think that's why you're here.

17:45.810 --> 17:49.410
I want a formal interview with you
and Gordon. I'll need your help with her.

17:49.810 --> 17:52.210
Yeah. All right.

17:52.510 --> 17:53.610
Um...

17:53.910 --> 17:56.110
How much sleep do you need, Kelvin?

17:56.510 --> 17:58.910
- How much sleep?
- Yeah.

17:59.210 --> 18:03.910
- How long can you go without sleep?
- Depends.

18:05.010 --> 18:06.210
Well,

18:06.610 --> 18:09.810
when you do go to sleep,

18:10.110 --> 18:15.110
I find I sleep much better
with the door locked.

18:17.810 --> 18:23.310
I was with the project when it was
still with NASA, before it was sold to DBA.

18:23.810 --> 18:25.710
I was trained in physics.

18:26.110 --> 18:30.510
I was sent here to assess
the economic potential of Solaris.

18:31.010 --> 18:36.610
Whether or not it was a viable commercial
property or possible energy source.

18:37.010 --> 18:41.110
I was still compiling data
when this shit started happening.

18:41.610 --> 18:44.210
Did you run any tests
on the food, air, water?

18:44.710 --> 18:51.310
I checked it 50 times. There are no signs of
contaminants or psychotropic compounds.

18:53.610 --> 18:57.710
How about you? How are you doing?

18:58.810 --> 19:00.510
Depression.

19:00.910 --> 19:05.510
Along with bouts of hypomania
and primary insomnia.

19:05.910 --> 19:09.610
Suggestions of agoraphobia,
obsessive-compulsive disorder,

19:10.010 --> 19:12.010
shock, fatigue, denial...

19:12.410 --> 19:16.110
- Not unusual, given the circumstances.
- I know.

19:16.510 --> 19:22.410
All right. Now, what can you tell me
about what's happening here?

19:22.910 --> 19:28.110
Just that I want it to stop,
but I want to stop it.

19:28.710 --> 19:34.010
If I can stop it that means
I'm smarter than it is.

19:39.210 --> 19:44.310
You know you can go home,
walk away from all of this.

19:44.710 --> 19:48.610
I can guarantee it.

19:54.210 --> 19:56.410
Yeah.

19:56.810 --> 20:02.510
The thing is... Man, I would kill
to go back there. I'd... kill.

20:03.010 --> 20:05.510
But Gordon?

20:05.810 --> 20:10.510
Gordon happens to be Gordon, you know?

20:10.910 --> 20:14.410
So, um...

20:18.310 --> 20:21.710
But I'll see what I can do.

20:22.110 --> 20:26.310
We take off into the cosmos.

20:26.910 --> 20:31.910
Ready for anything -
solitude, hardship, exhaustion...

20:32.410 --> 20:35.510
death.

20:36.810 --> 20:38.810
We're proud of ourselves.

20:39.110 --> 20:44.610
But when you think about it,
our enthusiasm's a sham.

20:47.710 --> 20:52.810
We don't want other worlds. We want mirrors.

23:40.910 --> 23:43.710
So, anyway... How's the spawn?

23:44.010 --> 23:47.410
Oh, good, good. He cries
and shits in his pants every two hours.

23:47.910 --> 23:51.410
I know the feeling.

23:51.710 --> 23:53.610
When are you leaving?

23:53.910 --> 23:57.410
- We've been postponed again.
- I didn't hear that.

23:57.910 --> 23:59.510
Nobody knows yet.

23:59.910 --> 24:04.110
The governments are looking for a buyer. I
wish we could tell people what's happening.

24:04.410 --> 24:06.510
You can tell me. I'm a doctor.

24:06.910 --> 24:10.710
Well, Doctor, as we study Solaris,

24:11.110 --> 24:15.110
the most interesting thing is it, um...

24:15.510 --> 24:20.010
Well, it seems to be reacting.
Almost like it knows it's being observed.

24:20.510 --> 24:23.010
We can't explain it.

24:23.410 --> 24:27.010
Are you listening to me? Chris?

24:28.610 --> 24:32.410
- So anyway...
- So anyway. Sorry.

24:32.910 --> 24:38.810
Go to her. Her name is Rheya. She's a bit
tricky but, um, I guess she's worthwhile.

24:39.410 --> 24:41.310
Maybe she needs a shrink.

24:41.710 --> 24:45.110
Don't we all?

25:30.010 --> 25:33.710
Don't blow it.

25:37.910 --> 25:39.410
You start.

25:39.710 --> 25:41.710
I did.

25:42.010 --> 25:43.610
Really?

25:43.910 --> 25:50.010
All right, I'm gonna resist the impulse
to ask you about the door knob.

25:50.410 --> 25:53.710
- Do you always resist your impulses?
- Not always.

25:55.710 --> 25:59.610
Try poetry.

26:00.210 --> 26:03.010
"And death shall have no dominion."

26:03.310 --> 26:06.910
Mm. Thomas.

26:07.410 --> 26:11.710
It's not a very happy poem, though.

26:11.910 --> 26:18.410
Well, you didn't seem
very happy when I saw you on the train.

26:21.910 --> 26:24.210
I wasn't.

26:24.610 --> 26:28.010
And tonight?

26:29.210 --> 26:32.910
It's early.

29:15.210 --> 29:18.610
Goddammit!

29:53.210 --> 29:55.610
I'm awake.

29:56.010 --> 29:59.210
Yes.

29:59.710 --> 30:01.810
How are you here?

30:02.110 --> 30:04.110
How are you here?

30:04.510 --> 30:07.810
How do you mean?

30:08.210 --> 30:14.710
Where do you think you are?
Where do you think you are right now?

30:15.410 --> 30:18.510
At home.

30:18.910 --> 30:22.810
Where is home?

30:23.210 --> 30:26.310
With you, where we live.

30:26.810 --> 30:33.710
And do you remember being anywhere else
with me? Being together anywhere else?

30:35.210 --> 30:39.710
- Our apartment.
- Describe it.

30:40.610 --> 30:44.910
It's dark. It's very very dark.

30:46.210 --> 30:50.310
And there are no paintings on the wall.

30:50.710 --> 30:54.010
No pictures anywhere.

30:54.310 --> 30:59.810
No pictures on the fridge, even,
which I always thought was a bit strange.

31:00.310 --> 31:05.510
Do you remember
where we first saw each other?

31:06.810 --> 31:10.510
On a train.

31:19.010 --> 31:22.110
Chris...

31:28.410 --> 31:32.410
I'm so happy to see you.

31:33.310 --> 31:37.210
I love you so much.

31:42.010 --> 31:46.310
Don't you love me any more?

31:49.810 --> 31:53.010
I have to check out something with the crew.

31:53.310 --> 31:54.910
No! No!

31:55.210 --> 32:00.210
- Don't leave me! Don't leave me!
- Why? Why?

32:01.510 --> 32:05.210
- Why?
- I don't know.

32:06.910 --> 32:10.410
I don't know.

32:12.710 --> 32:14.510
It's OK.

32:14.810 --> 32:18.310
It's OK.

32:27.010 --> 32:30.910
Why are you sitting over there?

32:34.510 --> 32:38.810
Can I come and sit with you?

33:57.710 --> 34:01.010
Hey.

34:04.110 --> 34:08.210
What was that?

34:10.110 --> 34:11.810
Yeah.

34:12.110 --> 34:15.310
How 'bout that?

34:15.810 --> 34:19.610
Still workin' on that.

34:22.610 --> 34:25.210
Where's your visitor?

34:25.710 --> 34:30.110
I don't know. Stopped appearing.

34:31.110 --> 34:35.310
- Who's your visitor?
- My brother.

34:54.310 --> 34:57.610
Who was it?

34:58.110 --> 35:01.610
My wife.

35:02.610 --> 35:05.710
Dead?

35:13.210 --> 35:17.110
So what was her name?

35:18.010 --> 35:21.910
Will she come back?

35:27.510 --> 35:31.110
Do you want her to?

36:29.210 --> 36:30.910
- No, it isn't.
- Yes, it is.

36:31.210 --> 36:34.210
- No, it isn't. It's crap.
- Only one way to find out.

36:34.510 --> 36:37.710
You can submit it to someone
and see if they publish it.

36:38.110 --> 36:40.310
That's not an indication of anything.

36:40.610 --> 36:45.210
So no one else's opinion counts
except for yours?

36:45.610 --> 36:48.810
- Yeah.
- That's insane.

36:49.210 --> 36:51.410
- "That's" insane.
- I like it.

36:51.710 --> 36:56.010
Brings out the red in my eyes.

36:58.710 --> 37:01.810
So, did you show it to your father?

37:02.210 --> 37:03.910
- Yeah.
- And?

37:04.210 --> 37:06.610
- And he liked it.
- What'd he say?

37:06.910 --> 37:10.910
- He said he liked it.
- Well...

37:11.510 --> 37:16.910
He's a man who doesn't pass out
compliments very easily. That's something.

37:17.310 --> 37:20.910
- What's that tell you?
- Can we talk about something else? Please?

37:21.310 --> 37:25.610
All right. When do you wanna get hitched?

37:28.210 --> 37:32.910
Every time I bring it up
you make a joke about it, and...

37:33.510 --> 37:37.610
I know, I know. That's pathet...
I'm sorry. It's just...

37:37.910 --> 37:39.810
It-it's so difficult for me.

37:40.110 --> 37:43.610
Still? Is it something that I'm not doing?

37:44.010 --> 37:47.010
No. No, no, no. That's not the issue at all.

37:47.310 --> 37:50.010
Because, you know,
if you keep putting this off,

37:50.310 --> 37:54.310
then in 15 or 20 years
I'm just gonna stop asking.

37:54.810 --> 37:58.910
- Well, I've got ages, then.
- Mm.

37:59.210 --> 38:04.210
So apart from the poem that you
quoted to me the night that we met...

38:04.610 --> 38:06.610
The night that you were hitting on me.

38:06.910 --> 38:09.910
Oh, I don't think so.
What's your favourite poem?

38:10.310 --> 38:13.710
My favourite Dylan Thomas poem?
Well, there's the, uh...

38:14.110 --> 38:17.410
Listen to this. We have, uh... There's the...

38:17.910 --> 38:20.210
Well, there's the one he's most famous for,

38:20.610 --> 38:23.710
which starts, um...

38:24.010 --> 38:28.410
- "There was a young man from Nantucket..."
- I knew it. I just...

38:28.810 --> 38:31.010
I'm not marrying you.

38:31.310 --> 38:34.410
You...

38:35.210 --> 38:39.010
Oh, you're marrying me.

38:49.210 --> 38:52.910
Would we have to invite anyone else?

38:53.210 --> 38:56.310
There should be witnesses.

38:56.810 --> 39:01.410
Otherwise nobody'd believe us.

39:03.710 --> 39:08.410
When I was little I had
this imaginary friend called Mikashelli,

39:08.910 --> 39:12.610
who used to live under the wallpaper
in the corner of the room.

39:13.010 --> 39:16.810
I used to go and visit. I had a very
intense relationship. I was an only child.

39:17.210 --> 39:20.610
As you know. And, um...
that was like my sibling.

39:21.010 --> 39:27.510
That was the person I used to have
battles with and fights with and everything.

39:28.010 --> 39:31.910
What happened progressively
over the next few years

39:32.410 --> 39:34.910
is that my mother stopped
communicating with me.

39:35.210 --> 39:40.310
She only communicated with me as
Mikashelli, and wrote me these letters,

39:40.910 --> 39:43.010
and we didn't have conversations any more.

39:43.310 --> 39:46.310
- I mean, admittedly, she was certifiable.
- Mm-hm.

39:46.610 --> 39:51.610
But, um, yeah, that was
a strange way to grow up.

39:52.110 --> 39:54.410
You know, you're with the right man.

39:54.710 --> 39:57.510
I so know that. That's what's great.

39:57.910 --> 40:01.410
Cos, man...

40:27.110 --> 40:29.710
Rheya...

40:30.010 --> 40:32.510
It's me.

40:32.910 --> 40:36.310
It's me.

40:40.010 --> 40:44.010
I don't remember that.

40:44.610 --> 40:48.510
When did you get that?

40:49.010 --> 40:51.910
I got it just before I came here.

40:52.310 --> 40:56.210
- Was I with you?
- No.

41:03.010 --> 41:07.110
I don't actually remember anything.

41:08.510 --> 41:12.410
I only remember you.

41:12.810 --> 41:16.710
Have I been ill?

41:18.310 --> 41:21.810
Sort of.

41:22.710 --> 41:24.710
And we've been apart?

41:25.010 --> 41:27.710
- Yes.
- For how long?

41:28.110 --> 41:31.810
A few years.

41:32.010 --> 41:35.110
- Were you alone?
- Yes.

41:35.510 --> 41:39.410
Was that difficult?

41:41.410 --> 41:45.910
It was easier than being with someone else.

41:46.110 --> 41:50.010
Did you think about me?

41:52.610 --> 41:55.810
Yes.

42:03.210 --> 42:06.510
What is that, out there?

42:06.910 --> 42:09.610
Solaris.

42:10.010 --> 42:13.510
Oh, my God, yes.

42:17.910 --> 42:21.010
I can't remember how I got here.

42:21.310 --> 42:25.410
Did I come here with you?

42:26.110 --> 42:31.110
- I don't know how you got here.
- What do you mean?

42:32.610 --> 42:37.210
I woke up and you were here.

42:37.910 --> 42:40.310
So I wasn't here yesterday?

42:40.710 --> 42:43.510
No.

42:44.210 --> 42:47.310
Right.

43:41.610 --> 43:45.210
Getting dressed?

43:46.110 --> 43:48.810
People will notice tonight.

43:49.110 --> 43:51.510
If you're not there, Rheya,

43:51.810 --> 43:55.410
people will notice.

43:58.510 --> 44:03.210
I can put up with all of it,
you know? The mood swings, the...

44:03.710 --> 44:05.310
restlessness,

44:05.610 --> 44:10.310
changing jobs every three months, all of it.

44:11.810 --> 44:14.910
What I can't put up with
is you hiding from me.

44:15.310 --> 44:19.110
Why do you do that?

44:22.510 --> 44:25.510
Do you wanna be here?

44:25.810 --> 44:32.110
Cos I need help. I can't do this...
I can't "continue" to do this on my own.

44:34.210 --> 44:37.810
The idea of God
was dreamed up by man.

44:38.110 --> 44:40.310
A silly animal with a small brain.

44:40.610 --> 44:43.610
Even the limits
that we put on it are human limits.

44:44.110 --> 44:48.610
- It designs, it creates...
- No, I'm talking about a higher intelligence.

44:49.110 --> 44:53.110
No, hold it. You're talking about
something else - a man in a white beard.

44:53.510 --> 44:56.810
Ascribing human characteristics
to something that isn't human.

44:57.110 --> 44:59.110
Aren't we all?

44:59.510 --> 45:03.810
Rheya, given all the elements
of the known universe and enough time,

45:04.210 --> 45:06.410
our existence is inevitable.

45:06.710 --> 45:10.110
It's no more mysterious than trees or sharks.

45:10.610 --> 45:14.610
We're a mathematical probability,
and that's all.

45:14.910 --> 45:17.610
How do you explain that
of all the creatures on this planet,

45:18.010 --> 45:20.510
only we are conscious of our own mortality?

45:20.910 --> 45:24.010
You can't explain that.
That doesn't mean there's a God.

45:24.310 --> 45:26.710
Maybe religion has been bred into us.

45:27.110 --> 45:29.110
The pope is a wonderful woman...

45:49.710 --> 45:53.210
- Excuse me.
- A nihilistic shrink. Is there a school?

45:53.510 --> 45:55.410
Not yet.

45:55.810 --> 45:57.610
You see? He's funny, at least.

46:12.410 --> 46:16.210
Where you been?

46:20.610 --> 46:24.910
Away from those fucking people.

46:25.910 --> 46:29.610
They're my friends.

46:31.610 --> 46:35.010
Yeah.

46:46.810 --> 46:50.610
Chris, I've got to talk to you.

46:52.610 --> 46:56.010
What's wrong?

46:56.810 --> 47:01.110
I don't understand what's happening.

47:01.710 --> 47:05.510
And if I do understand what's happening
then I don't think I can handle it.

47:06.010 --> 47:08.010
What do you mean?

47:08.410 --> 47:11.810
I mean...

47:12.710 --> 47:15.010
I mean...

47:15.310 --> 47:18.410
I'm not the person I remember.

47:18.710 --> 47:21.910
Or at least I'm not sure I am.

47:22.210 --> 47:28.710
I mean, l-I do remember things,
but I don't remember being there.

47:29.310 --> 47:32.810
I don't remember experiencing those things.

47:33.210 --> 47:36.510
My... I...

47:37.710 --> 47:40.210
I mean, I'm really really...

47:40.610 --> 47:43.010
really really trying to understand.

47:43.310 --> 47:46.110
And-and these, uh...

47:46.410 --> 47:50.610
These... these strange thoughts
keep coming into my head, and I...

47:51.010 --> 47:55.410
I don't know where they're
coming from, and I'm scared.

47:55.810 --> 47:56.910
Um...

47:57.310 --> 48:01.310
And l-I don't know what's happening.
L-I don't know what's happening.

48:01.810 --> 48:04.310
- What do you think's happening?
- You need rest.

48:04.610 --> 48:06.110
- No...
- Take that.

48:06.510 --> 48:11.110
You don't understand. Because
I don't think that I can live with this.

48:11.510 --> 48:16.010
I don't understand what is happening now.

48:17.410 --> 48:23.310
I mean, this-this-this... I remember this.
I have a memory of it. But...

48:24.710 --> 48:28.810
But I don't. I don't remember
seeing it. I don't...

48:29.110 --> 48:33.610
I don't remember being there. I...

48:35.910 --> 48:40.710
Rheya, it's fatigue. It's fatigue.
It's brought on by stress.

48:41.110 --> 48:44.510
It's fatigue. That's why you take this.

48:44.810 --> 48:47.610
Right. Yeah.

48:48.010 --> 48:51.710
No, it is. You'll be fine. I'll talk to Gordon
and Snow. We'll go back to Earth.

48:52.010 --> 48:53.910
- Mm-hm.
- And you're gonna be fine.

48:54.310 --> 48:56.710
Mm-hm.

48:57.010 --> 48:58.910
Mm.

48:59.310 --> 49:01.510
- I'm coming right back.
- Right.

49:01.910 --> 49:05.510
- Are you gonna be all right here?
- Yeah. Yeah.

49:06.010 --> 49:09.310
Yeah.

49:10.010 --> 49:13.110
This door locks from the inside.

49:13.510 --> 49:16.010
- Yeah.
- You'll be perfectly safe in here.

49:16.410 --> 49:17.810
Yeah.

49:18.210 --> 49:20.610
You sure you're gonna be all right?

49:20.910 --> 49:23.910
You-you keep asking me that,
actually. Yes. Yeah.

49:24.310 --> 49:27.110
I'm fine. I'm fine.

49:27.510 --> 49:30.410
Stay here.

49:52.410 --> 49:54.510
I was so worried, man.

49:54.910 --> 49:59.810
About this guy. But then you show up,
and I'm even more-more worried about you.

50:00.310 --> 50:04.410
Particularly after the first...
when you sent the first one away.

50:04.910 --> 50:07.810
Yeah, you were pretty...

50:08.210 --> 50:11.710
Pretty, uh... You deserved to be
as freaked out as you were.

50:12.110 --> 50:17.810
She can never know anything
about that. Ever. You understand?

50:22.610 --> 50:26.110
No, no, no, no, no.

50:27.110 --> 50:31.610
I wonder if they can get pregnant.

50:32.610 --> 50:34.510
Where are you going?

50:34.910 --> 50:37.310
- I can't be here.
- What?

50:37.610 --> 50:39.510
You should have told me.

50:39.910 --> 50:43.010
- It wouldn't have made any difference.
- Really?

50:43.410 --> 50:45.710
Chris, I had to!

50:46.010 --> 50:48.910
Obviously I had to. You know that about me.

50:49.210 --> 50:52.410
I had no idea you'd react like this. Listen!

50:52.910 --> 50:54.910
Listen to me.

50:55.210 --> 50:58.110
What's changed?
I didn't even know you wanted one.

50:58.410 --> 51:01.810
Yeah, why would I want one?
Why would I want a child,

51:02.110 --> 51:05.410
or anything that would
bring life into this house?!

51:05.810 --> 51:08.910
- No, no, Chris. No. No.
- Stop it. Stop it. Stop it.

51:09.210 --> 51:12.910
Stop it! Stop it!

51:13.310 --> 51:15.710
No, Chris, you don't understand.

51:16.010 --> 51:20.310
You have to understand. I had no idea you
felt like that. I won't make it without you.

51:20.810 --> 51:23.210
- Then you won't make it.
- Chris, no, please!

51:23.610 --> 51:25.710
- Let go of me!
- No...

51:26.110 --> 51:29.510
No!

51:32.310 --> 51:34.510
Oh, my God.

51:34.910 --> 51:36.610
Oh, no.

51:36.910 --> 51:40.710
You wanna change Gordon's mind.
What if Gordon and your wife, right,

51:41.010 --> 51:45.510
your very nice wife... She's nice, right?
Of course she's nice. Your wife is nice.

51:45.910 --> 51:50.610
They get together, right?
Cos I'm thinkin'... women, right?

51:51.210 --> 51:54.810
Right now we got woman and woman, right?

51:55.110 --> 51:59.210
If we get "women", you know, together on the
same team and all that shit, what happens?

51:59.610 --> 52:03.110
You know what happens.
All kinds of shit you can't explain happens.

52:03.510 --> 52:05.710
Like the... But good shit, you know?

52:06.010 --> 52:09.910
Mysterious, but good. Usually very good.
Things get solved, you know?

52:10.210 --> 52:15.310
That's my plan, you know?
What do you... think?

52:16.810 --> 52:20.710
I'll have to think about that.

52:27.510 --> 52:31.110
"And death shall have no dominion."

52:31.510 --> 52:34.210
"Dead men naked, they shall be one

52:34.610 --> 52:37.210
With the man in the wind
and the west moon. "

52:37.610 --> 52:42.010
"When their bones are picked clean
and the clean bones gone,

52:42.310 --> 52:45.710
They shall have stars at elbow and foot. "

52:46.110 --> 52:49.310
"Though they go mad they shall be sane."

52:49.610 --> 52:53.110
"Though they sink through the sea
they shall rise again. "

52:53.510 --> 52:56.910
"Though lovers be lost love shall not."

52:57.310 --> 53:01.810
"And death shall have no dominion."

53:44.510 --> 53:48.010
You found me.

53:50.310 --> 53:54.210
I came back for you.

53:54.910 --> 53:58.710
I came back that day.

54:06.310 --> 54:09.710
I'm sorry.

54:22.210 --> 54:24.610
All right. Enough hypothesising.

54:25.110 --> 54:28.710
The visitors. Are they or are they not
made of subatomic particles?

54:29.010 --> 54:30.910
Subatomic particles... I'm not sure.

54:31.310 --> 54:33.110
What do you think?

54:33.510 --> 54:35.610
I think... probably.

54:36.010 --> 54:39.810
Stabilised by what?

54:40.510 --> 54:43.210
Guess.

54:43.510 --> 54:47.610
I don't know. Maybe... a Higgs field.

54:48.110 --> 54:49.610
So...

54:49.910 --> 54:54.710
if we created a negative Higgs field and
bombarded them with Higgs antibosons

54:55.210 --> 54:57.310
they might disintegrate?

54:57.710 --> 55:00.910
Maybe. You know,
it would take a lot of power.

55:01.310 --> 55:04.210
Shut down all
the noncritical ship functions.

55:04.710 --> 55:08.010
This is just a theory,
you know? We could be wrong.

55:08.310 --> 55:13.110
- Let's find out.
- We'll take the findings back to Earth.

55:13.510 --> 55:16.210
What if they follow us back?

55:16.610 --> 55:20.110
What if what's happening here
happened on Earth on a mass scale?

55:20.410 --> 55:22.610
Don't you see that as a problem?

55:22.910 --> 55:25.510
I think it's a serious mistake
to assume it's benign.

55:25.910 --> 55:28.810
It's driving us crazy
so it can watch us kill each other.

55:29.310 --> 55:31.810
Is that really why you think they're here?

55:32.210 --> 55:38.510
Given its resources it could have
done anything, including destroy us.

55:39.410 --> 55:41.810
Meet me in the lab in an hour.

55:42.210 --> 55:44.010
- I won't let you.
- How you gonna stop us?

55:44.410 --> 55:49.210
- How you gonna stop me taking her back?
- Shall we pick up the other one on the way?

55:49.610 --> 55:55.010
Shouldn't be too hard. We could
chart its course. Only take a day or so.

55:55.610 --> 55:59.010
Chris, what's she talking about?

55:59.410 --> 56:02.610
- Nothing.
- Her oxygen might have run out.

56:03.010 --> 56:06.310
Maybe they don't need any.

56:06.610 --> 56:08.710
Chris, what are they talking about?

56:09.010 --> 56:11.010
You didn't tell her?

56:11.310 --> 56:14.410
Tell me what?

56:14.810 --> 56:18.610
Tell me what?

56:30.710 --> 56:35.210
- You came before.
- He got rid of you.

56:36.010 --> 56:39.610
You what?

56:41.110 --> 56:43.510
I sent you away.

56:43.910 --> 56:46.010
Into space.

56:46.310 --> 56:49.610
Oh, my God.

56:50.010 --> 56:52.110
Oh, my God.

56:52.410 --> 56:55.910
No. Rheya...

56:57.810 --> 56:59.410
Don't touch me.

56:59.710 --> 57:04.110
Rheya, I didn't understand.

57:04.810 --> 57:07.510
Rheya. Rheya. Hey.

57:07.810 --> 57:11.810
- Don't.
- No. No. No. Don't.

57:45.810 --> 57:50.910
What were you trying to
accomplish with that, exactly?

57:52.210 --> 57:55.710
Kelvin...

57:59.510 --> 58:04.410
It is a mistake to become
emotionally engaged with one of them.

58:05.010 --> 58:07.410
You're being manipulated.

58:07.810 --> 58:13.110
If she were ugly, you wouldn't want her
around. That's why she's not ugly.

58:13.610 --> 58:17.210
She's a mirror that reflects part
of your mind. You provide the formula.

58:17.610 --> 58:21.310
- She's alive.
- She is not human.

58:21.610 --> 58:24.410
Try to understand that,
if you can understand anything.

58:24.810 --> 58:30.310
What about your visitor? The one you're
so ready to destroy without hesitation?

58:30.810 --> 58:32.810
Who is it? "What" is it?

58:33.210 --> 58:36.110
Does it feel? Can it touch?

58:36.410 --> 58:40.110
Does it speak?

58:40.710 --> 58:46.110
We are in a situation
that is beyond morality. Hm?

58:46.310 --> 58:49.010
Your wife is dead.

58:49.510 --> 58:54.810
How do you know? How can you be definitive
about a construct you do not understand?

58:55.210 --> 58:57.810
She's a copy. A facsimile.

58:58.110 --> 59:01.310
And she's seducing you all over again.

59:01.710 --> 59:05.410
You're sick.

59:08.910 --> 59:13.110
We are not taking her back with us.

01:00:26.810 --> 01:00:30.510
Leave the light off.

01:00:42.410 --> 01:00:46.110
You think you're dreaming me.

01:00:46.510 --> 01:00:48.410
You're not Gibarian.

01:00:48.810 --> 01:00:51.310
No?

01:00:51.710 --> 01:00:54.710
Who am I, then?

01:00:55.110 --> 01:00:57.710
- A puppet.
- And you're not?

01:00:58.010 --> 01:01:00.410
Well, maybe you're my puppet.

01:01:00.710 --> 01:01:04.310
But like all puppets,
you think you're actually human.

01:01:04.710 --> 01:01:09.210
That's the puppet's dream - being human.

01:01:14.610 --> 01:01:17.310
Why did you kill yourself?

01:01:17.610 --> 01:01:21.310
It seemed like a good idea
at the time. Now I think I made a mistake.

01:01:21.810 --> 01:01:26.010
- What about your son?
- That's not my son. My son is on Earth.

01:01:26.410 --> 01:01:32.710
And that's not your wife.
They are part of Solaris. Remember that.

01:01:36.410 --> 01:01:39.210
What does Solaris want from us?

01:01:39.610 --> 01:01:42.910
Why do you think it has to want something?

01:01:43.310 --> 01:01:48.910
This is why you have to leave.
If you keep thinking there is a solution...

01:01:49.310 --> 01:01:51.710
you'll die here.

01:01:52.010 --> 01:01:54.610
I can't leave her.

01:01:54.810 --> 01:01:57.410
I'll figure it out.

01:01:57.710 --> 01:02:00.510
Do you understand
what I'm trying to tell you?

01:02:00.910 --> 01:02:03.210
There are no answers.

01:02:03.510 --> 01:02:07.210
Only choices.

01:02:26.810 --> 01:02:30.110
Rheya?

01:02:36.010 --> 01:02:39.310
Rheya?

01:02:50.510 --> 01:02:53.710
Rheya?

01:03:11.810 --> 01:03:15.110
Rheya?

01:03:21.510 --> 01:03:24.910
Gordon!

01:04:05.210 --> 01:04:10.210
- What happened?
- She drank liquid oxygen.

01:04:33.910 --> 01:04:37.410
She's dead.

01:04:38.210 --> 01:04:41.010
No.

01:05:02.110 --> 01:05:08.410
I never get used to them.
These... resurrections.

01:06:07.110 --> 01:06:10.510
Oh, no.

01:06:11.310 --> 01:06:14.510
No.

01:06:20.010 --> 01:06:23.810
Why'd you do that?

01:06:24.810 --> 01:06:26.010
Rheya?

01:06:26.310 --> 01:06:30.210
Don't call me that.

01:06:37.510 --> 01:06:40.110
There are two components.

01:06:40.410 --> 01:06:46.310
A high-energy proton accelerator
and a matter phase modulator.

01:06:46.810 --> 01:06:52.610
By adjusting the tuning frequency I get an
enhancement of Higgs antibosons at 90GHz

01:06:53.110 --> 01:06:57.010
and an almost pure beam at 160GHz.

01:06:57.410 --> 01:07:01.210
I used it on mine.

01:07:01.710 --> 01:07:03.410
What happens?

01:07:03.810 --> 01:07:08.610
They disappear,
back where they came from.

01:07:12.010 --> 01:07:15.710
It's what she wants.

01:07:16.310 --> 01:07:20.210
I won't let her do it.

01:07:20.510 --> 01:07:24.910
She'll come to me when you're asleep.

01:07:26.710 --> 01:07:30.710
Then I won't sleep.

01:07:32.710 --> 01:07:35.510
Don't you see?
I came from your memory of her.

01:07:35.910 --> 01:07:39.910
That's the problem. I'm not a whole person.

01:07:40.310 --> 01:07:44.810
In your memory
you get to control everything.

01:07:45.110 --> 01:07:49.710
So even if you remember something wrong,
I am predetermined to carry it out.

01:07:50.110 --> 01:07:52.510
I'm suicidal because
that's how you remember me.

01:07:52.810 --> 01:07:57.110
My voice sounds the way it does
because that's how you remember it.

01:07:57.610 --> 01:08:01.710
I don't believe that we're
predetermined to relive our past.

01:08:02.210 --> 01:08:06.410
I think that we can choose to do it differently.

01:08:06.810 --> 01:08:13.310
The day I left and you said you wouldn't make
it, I didn't hear you because I was angry.

01:08:13.910 --> 01:08:17.410
This is my chance to undo that mistake.

01:08:17.710 --> 01:08:20.110
And I need you to help me.

01:08:20.510 --> 01:08:24.710
But am I really Rheya?

01:08:28.310 --> 01:08:31.210
I don't know any more.

01:08:31.510 --> 01:08:35.910
All I see is you.

01:09:07.610 --> 01:09:11.410
All I see is you.

01:09:19.410 --> 01:09:23.010
It created me.

01:09:23.510 --> 01:09:27.810
And yet I can't communicate with it.

01:09:29.510 --> 01:09:32.110
It must hear me, though.

01:09:32.410 --> 01:09:36.710
It must know what's happening to me.

01:09:37.110 --> 01:09:41.210
And you and I, we would
have to have some kind of...

01:09:41.610 --> 01:09:45.710
an arrangement, some kind of...

01:09:49.310 --> 01:09:52.910
unspoken understanding...

01:09:53.210 --> 01:09:57.310
that I'm not really a human being.

01:09:59.410 --> 01:10:02.810
No, Rheya.

01:10:07.010 --> 01:10:08.910
Chris...

01:10:09.310 --> 01:10:13.310
Chris, I wish you would just
let them use the device on me.

01:10:13.710 --> 01:10:21.110
And then you can go back to Earth
and you can tell everybody all about Solaris.

01:10:23.410 --> 01:10:25.410
No.

01:10:25.710 --> 01:10:30.610
It's the only solution that makes any sense.

01:10:31.110 --> 01:10:35.110
We could never have
a life together on Earth, Chris.

01:10:35.510 --> 01:10:38.910
You know that.

01:10:39.210 --> 01:10:42.210
It would be impossible.

01:10:42.710 --> 01:10:46.810
And this? What kind of life is this?

01:10:47.210 --> 01:10:48.910
Trapped here.

01:10:49.310 --> 01:10:52.510
It's not a life.

01:10:52.910 --> 01:10:55.410
I don't know what to call it.

01:10:55.710 --> 01:10:59.010
It's what we have.

01:10:59.410 --> 01:11:01.410
It's enough for me.

01:11:01.710 --> 01:11:04.310
You need to rest.

01:11:04.710 --> 01:11:08.510
You're going to make yourself ill.

01:11:08.910 --> 01:11:14.210
- I don't care.
- Just lie down for a moment.

01:11:14.810 --> 01:11:16.510
Please, Chris.

01:11:16.810 --> 01:11:20.410
You have to rest.

01:11:49.410 --> 01:11:53.510
You know I'm not human
so I don't understand what you're afraid of.

01:11:54.010 --> 01:11:56.210
Of course you can use the device.

01:11:56.610 --> 01:11:59.810
It's not murder. You said that yourself.

01:12:00.210 --> 01:12:03.610
You're the one who had
the idea in the first place.

01:12:04.110 --> 01:12:08.110
Chris doesn't trust me. He...

01:17:01.010 --> 01:17:06.110
Chris, don't blame Gordon.

01:17:07.110 --> 01:17:11.510
It's not her fault. I begged her to do it.

01:17:12.510 --> 01:17:15.510
It's better this way.

01:17:16.010 --> 01:17:18.910
I found the suicide note.

01:17:19.210 --> 01:17:22.210
I went through your things.

01:17:22.510 --> 01:17:26.610
The page torn from the book of poems.

01:17:27.010 --> 01:17:30.810
And I realised...

01:17:31.110 --> 01:17:32.810
I'm not her.

01:17:33.210 --> 01:17:36.610
I'm not Rheya.

01:17:36.810 --> 01:17:39.710
I know you loved me, though.

01:17:40.110 --> 01:17:43.310
I know that. I felt that.

01:17:43.710 --> 01:17:46.110
And I love you.

01:17:46.510 --> 01:17:51.610
I wish we could just
live inside that feeling forever.

01:17:52.510 --> 01:17:56.410
Maybe there's a place where we can.

01:17:56.810 --> 01:17:58.910
But I know it's not on Earth.

01:17:59.210 --> 01:18:03.110
And it's not on this ship.

01:18:04.710 --> 01:18:08.610
That's all I can say right now.

01:18:30.510 --> 01:18:31.910
- You killed her!
- Not her. It.

01:18:32.210 --> 01:18:35.910
- It's murder!
- Kelvin, she begged me. It wasn't painful.

01:18:36.210 --> 01:18:37.510
- She'll be back!
- No.

01:18:37.810 --> 01:18:40.410
- Why would you let her do it?!
- Kelvin!

01:18:40.710 --> 01:18:42.510
It's not human!

01:18:42.810 --> 01:18:47.110
Whatever it is, it's not human,
and I'm threatened by that.

01:18:47.510 --> 01:18:50.210
And I wanna win. I want humans to win.

01:18:50.510 --> 01:18:54.310
Whose side are you on?

01:18:54.610 --> 01:19:01.110
- What are you doing?
- Putting the Al back online. I'm going home.

01:19:14.910 --> 01:19:18.210
Gordon.

01:19:19.610 --> 01:19:22.910
Gordon!

01:19:46.410 --> 01:19:49.810
- I knew it.
- How long you think he's been dead?

01:19:50.310 --> 01:19:54.710
Hard to say because of the cold.

01:19:55.010 --> 01:19:58.710
He attacked me.

01:20:00.310 --> 01:20:03.610
There I am. Somehow, there I am.

01:20:03.910 --> 01:20:09.410
And I couldn't tell you how I'm there,
or who I am or what's going on.

01:20:10.010 --> 01:20:13.310
But before I can get to that,

01:20:13.710 --> 01:20:15.810
what's this over here?

01:20:16.210 --> 01:20:19.610
Comin' at me. What...
what are you tryin' to do?

01:20:20.010 --> 01:20:23.010
Oh, I see. You're tryin' to kill me.

01:20:23.310 --> 01:20:27.210
Yeah, confusing. I'll tell you somethin'
confusing. Bingo, there you are,

01:20:27.610 --> 01:20:31.110
and my welcoming committee
dropped his knife and it's good night.

01:20:31.510 --> 01:20:35.710
And, oh, by the way, after all that I find, uh...

01:20:36.010 --> 01:20:40.610
this, uh, whoever this... I get my first
good look at it and it happens to be...

01:20:41.110 --> 01:20:44.010
I survive the first 30 seconds of this...

01:20:44.310 --> 01:20:48.110
life, whatever you wanna call it...
by killing someone.

01:20:48.510 --> 01:20:53.810
And, oh, ah, by killing someone
who happens to be me.

01:20:54.010 --> 01:20:58.910
See, most people... I would think most people
in this position would be, like "This... ah."

01:20:59.310 --> 01:21:03.810
"I don't know." However, this is at least...
This is an incredible opportunity.

01:21:04.310 --> 01:21:07.810
This is... What if this is a gift? I'm a gift.

01:21:08.210 --> 01:21:11.710
Hey.

01:21:13.910 --> 01:21:18.210
I say we use the Higgs device on him.

01:21:21.810 --> 01:21:24.110
Mm. Mm-mm.

01:21:24.410 --> 01:21:29.010
I don't think you really have time.

01:21:29.510 --> 01:21:33.210
Why would you say that?

01:21:33.510 --> 01:21:36.810
Well, you know, ever since
we used the famous Higgs device,

01:21:37.110 --> 01:21:42.010
Solaris started taking on mass exponentially.

01:21:42.410 --> 01:21:46.610
You might have noticed
how we're a lot closer to it.

01:21:46.910 --> 01:21:50.910
That would be because everything
within its gravitational field -

01:21:51.310 --> 01:21:55.210
it's pulling it in.

01:21:55.910 --> 01:21:58.010
Ah, and, yeah, sorry. By the way,

01:21:58.410 --> 01:22:04.410
the Higgs device also
drained the fuel cell reactors.

01:22:08.410 --> 01:22:12.210
Uh, if... Can I make a suggestion?

01:22:12.610 --> 01:22:17.410
I mean, this is... You can do what you want,
but I would just lock me in here really tight

01:22:17.810 --> 01:22:21.910
and take the "Athena" back.

01:22:24.510 --> 01:22:28.410
Wear your seat belt.

01:23:25.610 --> 01:23:28.010
Switch to internal power.

01:23:28.410 --> 01:23:31.710
Start fuel cell operational diagnostic.

01:23:32.010 --> 01:23:34.910
Service check on LGA.

01:23:35.310 --> 01:23:38.310
Point and calibrate high-beam antenna.

01:23:38.610 --> 01:23:42.110
Depressurising. Spin all turbines to standby.

01:23:42.610 --> 01:23:45.910
Disengage coupling interlocks
and all docking couplers.

01:23:46.210 --> 01:23:51.010
Vent and seal
all main engine propellant lines.

01:24:07.610 --> 01:24:10.110
Earth.

01:24:10.410 --> 01:24:14.110
Even the word sounded strange to me now.

01:24:14.610 --> 01:24:18.010
Unfamiliar.

01:24:20.410 --> 01:24:23.410
How long had I been gone?

01:24:23.910 --> 01:24:26.910
How long had I been back?

01:24:27.310 --> 01:24:30.910
Did it matter?

01:24:34.310 --> 01:24:39.610
I tried to find the rhythm
of the world where I used to live.

01:24:40.010 --> 01:24:42.810
I followed the current.

01:24:43.310 --> 01:24:47.010
I was silent and attentive.

01:24:47.310 --> 01:24:50.910
I made a conscious effort to smile...

01:24:51.310 --> 01:24:53.210
nod...

01:24:53.610 --> 01:24:55.910
stand...

01:24:56.210 --> 01:25:02.510
and perform the millions of gestures
that constitute life on Earth.

01:25:04.310 --> 01:25:10.010
I studied these gestures
until they became reflexes again.

01:25:11.710 --> 01:25:14.310
But I was haunted by the idea

01:25:14.810 --> 01:25:18.710
that I remembered her wrong.

01:25:21.110 --> 01:25:25.510
That somehow I was wrong about everything.

01:26:29.110 --> 01:26:33.910
Depressurising.
Spin all turbines to standby.

01:26:34.310 --> 01:26:38.110
Disengage coupling interlocks
and all docking couplers.

01:26:38.510 --> 01:26:43.310
Vent and seal
all main engine propellant lines.

01:27:46.610 --> 01:27:49.110
Rheya!

01:27:56.910 --> 01:28:00.310
Rheya?

01:30:13.410 --> 01:30:16.910
Chris?

01:30:17.310 --> 01:30:20.610
Chris?

01:31:00.310 --> 01:31:04.610
Am I alive... or dead?

01:31:07.010 --> 01:31:11.410
We don't have to think like that any more.

01:31:14.210 --> 01:31:18.010
We're together now.

01:31:19.310 --> 01:31:23.310
Everything we've done is forgiven.

01:31:23.710 --> 01:31:27.010
Everything.
